CROSS REFERENCE MATRIX - NH-148B EXTENSION PROJECT

CLAIM DOCUMENT → EVIDENCE → PRECEDENT → STANDARDS

Claim No. 1: Utility Shifting Delay (₹4.12 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Standing Committee Minutes (30.11.2021)
├─ Evidence: Contractor's Letters RC/2020/156, RC/2021/089, RC/2021/145
├─ Evidence: Site photographs (November 2020-May 2021)
├─ Precedent: BSNL v. Motorola (utility shifting = Employer's responsibility)
├─ Precedent: Simplex Infra v. NHAI (utility delay = compensable EOT)
└─ Standard: NHAI GCC Clause 44 (Employer's Responsibilities)

Claim No. 2: Forest Clearance Delay (₹3.87 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Forest Department letters
├─ Evidence: NHAI forwarding letters
├─ Evidence: Contractor's site reports
├─ Precedent: O.P. Bhasin v. HSIDC (statutory delays = Employer's responsibility)
└─ Standard: Forest Conservation Act 1980, NHAI GCC Clause 44

Claim No. 3: Price Escalation (₹6.43 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Material purchase invoices
├─ Evidence: Market price certificates
├─ Evidence: Steel Authority of India price lists
├─ Precedent: ONGC v. Modern Construction (price escalation methodology)
└─ Standard: NHAI GCC Clause 10CA (Price Escalation)

Claim No. 4: Variation VO-001 (₹4.92 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Revised alignment drawings
├─ Evidence: Joint Measurement Books
├─ Evidence: Site execution records
├─ Precedent: ONGC v. Modern Construction (variation rate computation)
└─ Standard: NHAI GCC Clause 12 (Variations)

Claim No. 5: Wrongful Termination (₹3.84 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Suspension Notice (15.04.2022)
├─ Evidence: Termination Notice (01.06.2022)
├─ Evidence: Unpaid running bills
├─ Precedent: FIDIC Clause 16 rights (suspension for non-payment)
└─ Standard: FIDIC Red Book 2017 Sub-Clause 16, NHAI GCC Clause 62

Claim No. 6: Unpaid Running Bills (₹2.14 Cr)
├─ Evidence: Certified RA Bills 45, 46, 47
├─ Evidence: Payment status records
└─ Standard: NHAI GCC Clause 7 (Running Bills)

